WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.916 --> 00:00:15.518
the boys returned in their pajamas, they all sang and danced.

2
00:00:16.838 --> 00:00:19.739
Soon their dancing turned into a noisy pillow fight.

3
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.621
Wendy quieted them and told them it was time for a good-night story.

4
00:00:25.802 --> 00:00:30.464
She would tell them the story they loved best, but it was a story that Peter hated.

5
00:00:32.228 --> 00:00:37.533
Usually when she told this story, Peter would put his hands over his ears or leave the room.

6
00:00:38.574 --> 00:00:40.535
But tonight he remained on his stool.

7
00:00:41.496 --> 00:00:48.582
This story was closest to Wendy's heart, and it began like this: "Once upon a time, there was

8
00:00:48.642 --> 00:00:49.923
a man called Mr.

9
00:00:49.963 --> 00:00:53.786
Darling and he lived with a woman called Mrs.

10
00:00:53.826 --> 00:00:57.810
Darling." "I knew them," John interrupted.

11
00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:01.933
"I think I knew them too," Michael joined in.

12
00:01:01.953 --> 00:01:09.299
"They lived in a big house in London," Wendy continued, "and had three darling children.

13
00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:12.842
The children had a faithful nanny called Nana.

14
00:01:14.524 --> 00:01:16.245
But one evening, Mr.

15
00:01:16.285 --> 00:01:20.169
Darling was angry with Nana and chained her up in the yard.

16
00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:23.412
So the three children flew away."

17
00:01:23.432 --> 00:01:28.076
"This is a really good story," said Nibs.

18
00:01:29.196 --> 00:01:34.838
"They flew away to Neverland where the lost children live," continued Wendy.

19
00:01:34.858 --> 00:01:37.438
"That's us!"

20
00:01:38.199 --> 00:01:40.019
cried the Lost Boys, excited.

21
00:01:40.039 --> 00:01:45.381
"And was one of the lost children called Tootles?"

22
00:01:46.281 --> 00:01:49.582
asked Tootles, who already knew the story well.

23
00:01:49.602 --> 00:01:52.543
"Yes," replied Wendy.

24
00:01:52.563 --> 00:01:57.144
"But the parents were very sad that their children had flown away.

25
00:01:58.472 --> 00:02:02.915
And they visited the nursery every night waiting for their children to return."

26
00:02:02.935 --> 00:02:06.338
"This is a sad story.

27
00:02:06.358 --> 00:02:12.683
I don't see how it can have a happy ending," said Nibs, forgetting what followed.

28
00:02:12.703 --> 00:02:15.565
"Don't worry," said Wendy.

29
00:02:15.585 --> 00:02:22.570
"It turns out all right at the end because the children knew their mother would always leave the

30
00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:25.132
window open for them to fly back home.

31
00:02:26.916 --> 00:02:28.457
Mothers are loyal like that.

32
00:02:29.458 --> 00:02:35.482
And because the children knew this, they stayed away for a long time and had fun."

33
00:02:36.483 --> 00:02:39.445
"Did they ever go back home to their parents?"

34
00:02:40.246 --> 00:02:40.926
asked the boys.

35
00:02:42.227 --> 00:02:44.969
This was the part of the story that Peter really hated.

36
00:02:44.989 --> 00:02:53.556
"Yes. One day, they decided to fly back to the open nursery window," Wendy said.

37
00:02:54.708 --> 00:02:57.749
"Their mother and father greeted them with much love.

38
00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:01.211
They didn't even scold them for running away.

39
00:03:02.431 --> 00:03:06.033
And the whole family lived happily ever after."

40
00:03:08.334 --> 00:03:13.616
That was the story and everyone was very pleased with its ending—except for Peter.

41
00:03:14.696 --> 00:03:15.837
He hated grown-ups.

42
00:03:16.817 --> 00:03:19.138
He had his own story to tell about mothers.

43
00:03:19.158 --> 00:03:24.040
"Wendy, you are wrong about mothers," he said.

44
00:03:24.992 --> 00:03:29.973
And the boys gathered around him to hear his story—one that he had never told before.

45
00:03:29.993 --> 00:03:39.416
"Long ago," he told them, "I thought—like you, Wendy— that my mother would always keep the window open

46
00:03:39.476 --> 00:03:39.816
for me.

47
00:03:40.916 --> 00:03:43.737
So I stayed away for many moons and suns.

48
00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:47.858
Then I flew back, but the window was locked.

49
00:03:48.918 --> 00:03:50.639
My mother had forgotten about me.

50
00:03:51.759 --> 00:03:54.580
And there was another little boy sleeping in my bed."

51
00:03:56.296 --> 00:04:01.880
This tale scared all the boys, especially John and Michael, who had been listening closely.

52
00:04:02.861 --> 00:04:07.464
The Lost Boys had been away from their mothers for a long time and so knew how to

53
00:04:07.524 --> 00:04:08.285
live without them.

54
00:04:09.145 --> 00:04:10.987
But John and Michael didn't know how.

55
00:04:11.007 --> 00:04:16.010
"Wendy, let's go home," they both cried.

56
00:04:17.431 --> 00:04:20.714
Wendy put her arms around them and thought about their request for a moment.

57
00:04:20.734 --> 00:04:23.496
"Yes," she said.

58
00:04:24.128 --> 00:04:26.910
"Maybe it is time to go home to our parents."

59
00:04:27.991 --> 00:04:30.412
The Lost Boys were shocked by this quick decision.

60
00:04:30.432 --> 00:04:34.255
"Tonight?" they asked, confused.

61
00:04:35.516 --> 00:04:38.017
"Yes, at once," Wendy replied.

62
00:04:39.138 --> 00:04:43.601
Suddenly an image of her mother crying in the empty nursery came to her mind.

63
00:04:44.522 --> 00:04:47.684
Peter, of course, refused to show his feelings to the group.

64
00:04:48.724 --> 00:04:56.336
Though he cared very much, he said coolly to Wendy, "If you wish, I'll make the necessary arrangements."

65
00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:00.751
But, in his heart of hearts, he wanted to cry.
